#  Protein-Protein Interaction (PPI) Network Analysis – TP53

> **Exploring the functional interaction network of the human TP53 tumor-suppressor protein using the STRING database.**

This project explores the **protein-protein interaction network of TP53** to understand how it is functionally connected with other proteins involved in **DNA damage response, cell-cycle regulation, DNA repair, transcription, and apoptosis**.

The analysis was performed using the **STRING database**, which helps visualize and investigate known and predicted functional associations between proteins.

---

##  Methodology & Database Configuration

###  Analysis Setup

- **Target Protein:** TP53 (Cellular tumor antigen p53)
- **Organism:** *Homo sapiens*
- **Database:** STRING
- **Interaction Sources:** Experimental evidence, curated databases, text mining, co-expression, and genomic context
- **Confidence Score:** Medium confidence (≥ 0.400)

